==German==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|wërden}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|werdan}}. Cognate with Dutch {{term|worden}}, Swedish {{term|varda}} and obsolete English verb {{term|worth||to become}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-werden.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|wird|wurde|geworden|past participle 2=worden|auxiliary=sein}}

# {{auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle {{term|geworden|lang=de}}|lang=de}} [[will]]; to be going (to do something); {{non-gloss definition|forms the future tense}}
#: ''Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.'' 
#:: I '''will''' go home.
# {{auxiliary|with a past participle|past participle {{term|worden|lang=de}}|lang=de}} to be done; {{non-gloss definition|forms the passive voice}}
#: ''Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen.''
#:: The book is '''being''' read.
#: ''Er war geschlagen '''worden'''.''
#:: He had '''been''' beaten.
# {{intransitive|past participle: “[[geworden]]”}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: ''Es '''wird''' heißer.''
#:: It's '''getting''' hotter.

